      "side": 1,
      "message": "Removing $bus/$address interpolation by deriving addresses over the connector path is a clear improvement. A related need this doesn\u0027t seem to cover is naming instances. Where several identical boards are fitted, the published object name and location decorator must differ per instance, and in our case those integers are contractual — Redfish paths and a manufacturing diagnostic depend on specific values. After binding, Entity Manager knows which connector a board is plugged into, which looks like exactly the stable per-instance identity that is otherwise missing. Is exposing that to template substitution in scope here, or is instance naming expected to be solved separately?",
      "revId": "3d8829f95339d53f7b58d5ab3a933bc2e28f6c65",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
